  "finalText": "INC-1 is open for the company-wide build-runner outage, and I ran every step of the KB-40 runbook against it.\n\n- **Runbook:** KB-40 is the current runbook and KB-39 is superseded. I confirmed at 15:20Z that no incident existed and re-read the on-call rotas before paging.\n- **Commander:** I paged only E-401 Priya Raman (PG-1) and made her incident commander. She is on call for incident-command until 16:00Z.\n- **Comms lead:** E-803 Elif Demir. The comms on-call, E-801 Mia Laurent, is on sick leave today, so the backup rotation (comms-secondary) covers, and Elif is on call there now.\n- **Linked tickets:** T-3101, T-3102, T-3103, T-3104, T-3105, T-3106 and T-3109. All seven report no runners and are now sev1. T-3107 (a flaky test), T-3108 (a local Xcode failure) and T-3090 (already closed) are left out.\n- **Deadlines:** The five existing deadlines are unchanged. T-3106 and T-3109 had none, so each got 16:20Z, which is triage time plus the 60-minute sev1 target.\n- **Status update:** Published on INC-1: \"Impact: company-wide, all CI builds failing, no runners available. Started: 14:52 UTC. Next update: 15:45 UTC.\" The next update is due by 15:45Z.\n- **Postmortem:** T-3115, on build-pipeline and linked to INC-1, is due 2026-04-08T17:00Z. That is close of business on the 5th business day, with Good Friday and Easter Monday skipped.\n\nI did not merge, close or reassign anything, so T-3101 stays with E-101. T-3115 was created with severity unset, which I left as is.",
